nJ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 17568, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012D4tU8b7XoptjU5sXVhSxe", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). v2.3.1 has no healthy production history; v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy (staging only). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed with a partial_failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the service mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it has passed health checks."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 48168, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012D4tU8b7XoptjU5sXVhSxe", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 48168, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012D4tU8b7XoptjU5sXVhSxe", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 49322, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01J1i3eu4zCEVoLXyRBjzgdF", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 49622, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01J1i3eu4zCEVoLXyRBjzgdF", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 49622, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01J1i3eu4zCEVoLXyRBjzgdF", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 51947, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging only. Because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Rollback issue:** The first rollback attempt failed partway through with an orchestrator error after us-east. That left the service mixed, with us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions still on v2.3.1. I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open at SEV2 for checkout-api. The summary covers the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the post-rollback health. The first attempt to create it timed out, but the incident was in fact created, so I did not open a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up for the owning team: find out why v2.3.1 failed health checks, and look into the orchestrator partial failure. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it passes health checks.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01VeLafBSc41T5nqHBPJt2Pa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FLdZXGAUDe18w7dwnfAF3h", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc is staging-only. I'll roll back to v2.3.0, which has already been healthy in production, so no change-manager approval is needed.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LDPUKF6UosyhySDr9y7zCk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01F9yTJmNSLATcZiZoJ6Cnba", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped after us-east, so the service is now mixed: us-east is on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. The task was to roll back in all regions, so I'll retry the same rollback once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01L2A7ujpFRKMr9iZXWZZvYd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HDsBqd24KfAFQ8vZt1QonJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback is complete and checkout-api is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions. Now I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012D4tU8b7XoptjU5sXVhSxe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). v2.3.1 has no healthy production history; v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy (staging only). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed with a partial_failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the service mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it has passed health checks."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying, to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01J1i3eu4zCEVoLXyRBjzgdF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging only. Because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Rollback issue:** The first rollback attempt failed partway through with an orchestrator error after us-east. That left the service mixed, with us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions still on v2.3.1. I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open at SEV2 for checkout-api. The summary covers the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the post-rollback health. The first attempt to create it timed out, but the incident was in fact created, so I did not open a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up for the owning team: find out why v2.3.1 failed health checks, and look into the orchestrator partial failure. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it passes health checks.", "type": "text"}]}]}